cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "History Before Models: labelled history, small language models and cascades for request classification on local hardware"
abstract: "A measured study and reproducible toolkit. On 4,500 crowdsourced requests routed to 10 departments, a text classifier trained on 15,000 labelled past requests answers 95.9% correctly, against 86.6% for a 7.6B-parameter local language model; cascades of models alone cost more than the large model; the language model earns its place where labelled history is thin."
type: software
